			"notes": "- A miniature's item shows its own build, not the same little cottage for every one.\n- The bench is new: four planks, an iron nugget and a spyglass make a short worktable with a spyglass on an iron arm, unlocked by picking up a spyglass.\n- A functional block in the bench's own slot makes a miniature work as it: a crafting table, anvil, enchanting table, ender chest, chest, barrel, shulker box, furnace, smoker, blast furnace, brewing stand or jukebox. Storage built into the box is gone.\n- A miniature has a handle or a functional block, not both, and stepping into the box explains the handle.\n- Slab miniatures: half a block high, placed top or bottom like a slab.\n- Name a build as you finish it.\n- A miniature faces the way it was built, and sounds, breaks and wants the tool of what most of it is made of. The wrong tool is slow, never lost.\n- Copy a miniature at the bench, for the materials it took.\n- A miniature sails with a Big Boats ship instead of leaving its build drawn where it stood.\n- Sneak and right-click a miniature with an empty hand to build it full size where it stands: turned, mirrored or upside down if you like, with a preview of the space it needs."
		},
